    {
     "type": "note",
     "title": "Bonus: word order",
     "md": "In English the order shows who is the subject. In German the **case** shows it — so the object can come first to emphasise it. The verb stays in **position 2**:\n\n- {de:Der Mann schreibt einen Brief.}\n- {de:Einen Brief schreibt der Mann.} (emphasis on *a letter* — not very common)"
    },
